        "description": {
          "value": "<p><em>Intelligence Saving Throw:</em> DC [[lookup @save.dc.value activity=JR6me2wr12iyyARj]], one Small or Medium creature within 5 feet that has the &amp;Reference[Incapacitated apply=false] condition, is a Humanoid or Beast, and has 10 Hit Points or fewer. <em>Failure:</em> The [[lookup @name lowercase]]{monster} possesses the target: it devours the target’s brain and teleports inside its skull. While there, the [[lookup @name lowercase]]{monster} has Total Cover against attacks and other effects originating outside its host. It keeps its own Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores, its understanding of Deep Speech, its telepathy and its Detect Intelligence trait, but otherwise uses the target’s game statistics, and it knows everything the target knew, including spells and languages. The [[lookup @name lowercase]]{monster} must leave the body if the host dies, and it is also forced out if the host regains its devoured brain through a <em>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWish000000]{Wish}</em> spell. By spending 5 feet of its movement, the [[lookup @name lowercase]]{monster} can leave the body voluntarily, teleporting to the nearest unoccupied space within 5 feet of it; the body then dies unless its brain is restored before the end of the [[lookup @name lowercase]]{monster}’s next turn.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
